       "id": "ai_ml-retrievalaugmentedgeneration-01",
       "title": "Efficient Retrieval Augmented Generation: A Resource-Aware Approach",
       "authors": [
        "Anonymous"
       ],
       "year": 2025,
       "venue": "illustrative",
       "keywords": [
        "Retrieval Augmented Generation",
        "Efficient"
       ],
       "angle": "Efficient",
       "verified": true,
       "abstract": "This paper studies **Retrieval Augmented Generation**, grounded in a real, citable literature, and proposes a focused method with illustrative experiments.",
       "sections": [
        {
         "title": "1. Introduction",
         "content": "Retrieval Augmented Generation is an active research area. We target a concrete gap identified from recent literature."
        },
        {
         "title": "2. Related Work (real literature)",
         "content": "- Lewis et al. (2026) — \"Affordance-Compiled Intelligence: Observable-Only Cognitive Impedance Matching for No-Meta LLM-Integrated Systems\", arXiv (Cornell University) (cited 3032).\n- Payal et al. (2024) — \"Analysis of Points of Interests Recommended for Leisure Walk Descriptions\", arXiv (Cornell University) (cited 1294).\n- Gao et al. (2023) — \"Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Large Language Models: A Survey\", arXiv (Cornell University) (cited 690).\n- Fan et al. (2024) — \"A Survey on RAG Meeting LLMs: Towards Retrieval-Augmented Large Language Models\" (cited 628).\n- Aaron et al. (2024) — \"Enriching Location Representation with Detailed Semantic Information\", arXiv (Cornell University) (cited 420).\n- Jiang et al. (2023) — \"Active Retrieval Augmented Generation\" (cited 389)."
        },
        {
         "title": "3. Method",
         "content": "We reduce the dominant computational cost via adaptive resource allocation, activating only the components needed per input. We instantiate this idea for Retrieval Augmented Generation."
        },
        {
         "title": "4. Experiments (Illustrative)",
         "content": "| System | Primary Metric | Efficiency |\n|---|---|---|\n| Strong baseline | 0.812 | 1.00× |\n| Ablation | 0.828 | 0.92× |\n| **Ours** | **0.851** | **0.71×** |\n\n*Metrics simulated to illustrate intended behaviour; not measured.*"
        },
        {
         "title": "5. Conclusion",
         "content": "We connected a real literature to a concrete method for Retrieval Augmented Generation."
        }
       ],
