       "id": "ai_ml-federatedlearningprivacy-01",
       "title": "Efficient Federated Learning Privacy: A Resource-Aware Approach",
       "authors": [
        "Anonymous"
       ],
       "year": 2025,
       "venue": "illustrative",
       "keywords": [
        "Federated Learning Privacy",
        "Efficient"
       ],
       "angle": "Efficient",
       "verified": true,
       "abstract": "This paper studies **Federated Learning Privacy**, grounded in a real, citable literature, and proposes a focused method with illustrative experiments.",
       "sections": [
        {
         "title": "1. Introduction",
         "content": "Federated Learning Privacy is an active research area. We target a concrete gap identified from recent literature."
        },
        {
         "title": "2. Related Work (real literature)",
         "content": "- Yang et al. (2019) — \"Federated Machine Learning\", ACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology (cited 6001).\n- McMahan et al. (2016) — \"Communication-Efficient Learning of Deep Networks from Decentralized\\n Data\", arXiv (Cornell University) (cited 5644).\n- McMahan et al. (2016) — \"Communication-Efficient Learning of Deep Networks from Decentralized Data\", arXiv (Cornell University) (cited 5178).\n- Kairouz et al. (2020) — \"Advances and Open Problems in Federated Learning\", Foundations and Trends® in Machine Learning (cited 4979).\n- Li et al. (2020) — \"Federated Learning: Challenges, Methods, and Future Directions\", IEEE Signal Processing Magazine (cited 4763).\n- Bonawitz et al. (2017) — \"Practical Secure Aggregation for Privacy-Preserving Machine Learning\" (cited 3541)."
        },
        {
         "title": "3. Method",
         "content": "We reduce the dominant computational cost via adaptive resource allocation, activating only the components needed per input. We instantiate this idea for Federated Learning Privacy."
        },
        {
         "title": "4. Experiments (Illustrative)",
         "content": "| System | Primary Metric | Efficiency |\n|---|---|---|\n| Strong baseline | 0.812 | 1.00× |\n| Ablation | 0.828 | 0.92× |\n| **Ours** | **0.851** | **0.71×** |\n\n*Metrics simulated to illustrate intended behaviour; not measured.*"
        },
        {
         "title": "5. Conclusion",
         "content": "We connected a real literature to a concrete method for Federated Learning Privacy."
        }
       ],
