       "title": "Scalable Rare Variant Burden Analysis for Large-Scale Settings",
       "authors": [
        "Anonymous"
       ],
       "year": 2025,
       "venue": "illustrative",
       "keywords": [
        "Rare Variant Burden Analysis",
        "Scalable"
       ],
       "angle": "Scalable",
       "verified": true,
       "abstract": "This paper studies **Rare Variant Burden Analysis**, grounded in a real, citable literature, and proposes a focused method with illustrative experiments.",
       "sections": [
        {
         "title": "1. Introduction",
         "content": "Rare Variant Burden Analysis is an active research area. We target a concrete gap identified from recent literature."
        },
        {
         "title": "2. Related Work (real literature)",
         "content": "- Wild (2005) — \"Complementing the Genome with an “Exposome”: The Outstanding Challenge of Environmental Exposure Measurement in Molecular Epidemiology\", Cancer Epidemiology Biomarkers & Prevention (cited 2482).\n- Rinella et al. (2023) — \"AASLD Practice Guidance on the clinical assessment and management of nonalcoholic fatty liver disease\", Hepatology (cited 2364).\n- Planchard et al. (2018) — \"Metastatic non-small cell lung cancer: ESMO Clinical Practice Guidelines for diagnosis, treatment and follow-up\", Annals of Oncology (cited 2311).\n- Pinto et al. (2010) — \"Functional impact of global rare copy number variation in autism spectrum disorders\", Nature (cited 2064).\n- Scuteri et al. (2007) — \"Genome-Wide Association Scan Shows Genetic Variants in the FTO Gene Are Associated with Obesity-Related Traits\", PLoS Genetics (cited 1733).\n- Wojcik et al. (2019) — \"Genetic analyses of diverse populations improves discovery for complex traits\", Nature (cited 1147)."
        },
        {
         "title": "3. Method",
         "content": "We decompose the problem across shards with a communication-efficient aggregation rule that keeps overhead sublinear in scale. We instantiate this idea for Rare Variant Burden Analysis."
        },
        {
         "title": "4. Experiments (Illustrative)",
         "content": "| System | Primary Metric | Efficiency |\n|---|---|---|\n| Strong baseline | 0.812 | 1.00× |\n| Ablation | 0.828 | 0.92× |\n| **Ours** | **0.851** | **0.71×** |\n\n*Metrics simulated to illustrate intended behaviour; not measured.*"
        },
        {
         "title": "5. Conclusion",
         "content": "We connected a real literature to a concrete method for Rare Variant Burden Analysis."
        }
       ],
